WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:02.840
Three working rules.

3
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.045
First, when someone cites scaling laws, ask which quantity was measured.

4
00:00:07.325 --> 00:00:13.512
Loss curves are well established; claims about tasks, jobs, or dates are extrapolations from them.

5
00:00:13.792 --> 00:00:28.235
Second, remember that the scaling story now has several axes: pretraining, reinforcement learning on checkable tasks, and test-time compute, each with its own cost curve, and the last one is a dial you control through effort settings.

6
00:00:28.515 --> 00:00:37.453
Third, when you hear “scaling is over” or “progress is accelerating,” find the date, the speaker’s incentives, and the specific measurement behind it.

7
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:40.464
The next lesson looks at those measurements directly.
